And here's an example to read a file line by line and calculate moving average for the last three numerical fields in each line using C#:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string[] lines = File.ReadAllLines("inputfile.txt");

        foreach (string line in lines)
        {
            // Split the line into fields separated by spaces or tabs
            string[] fields = line.Split(new char[] { ' ', '\t' }, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);

            if (fields.Length < 3)
                continue;   // Less than 3 numerical fields in this line

            double sum = 0;
            int count = 0;

            for (int i = fields.Length - 1; i >= 0 && count < 3; --i)
            {
                if (!Double.TryParse(fields[i], out double number))
                    continue;   // Non-numeric field, skip it

                sum += number;
                ++count;
            }

            if (count == 0)
                continue;   // No numeric fields in this line

            double movingAverage = sum / count;

            Console.WriteLine("Moving average of last three numerical fields: " + movingAverage);
        }
    }
}
``` 
Remember, you would need to add error handling and additional features according to your needs. Also these codes are basic examples and don't cover advanced topics such as concurrency issues, network latency handling etc. It will be much more complex and lengthy code for a complete solution.
