['This task involves designing a complex system which is beyond the capabilities of an AI model due to its complexity. However, I can provide you with an outline of how such a system might be architected and implemented in C++:

1. **Message Broker**: The message broker can be implemented using a Producer-Consumer pattern where messages are produced by producers (services that send data) and consumed by consumers (services that process the data). A thread safe queue can be used to store these messages. 

```cpp
#include <queue>
#include <mutex>
#include <condition_variable>

template<typename T>
class ThreadSafeQueue {
public:
    void push(T const& value) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mMutex);
        mData.push(value);
        mCondVar.notify_one();
    }

    bool tryPop(T& value) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mMutex);
        if(mData.empty()) return false;

        value = mData.front();
        mData.pop();
        return true;
    }

    void waitPop(T& value) {
        std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(mMutex);
        while(mData.empty()) {
            mCondVar.wait(lock);
        }

        value = mData.front();
        mData.pop();
    }

private:
    std::queue<T> mData;
    mutable std::mutex mMutex;
    std::condition_variable mCondVar;
};
```
2. **RESTful API**: The RESTful API can be implemented using a web framework like Restbed or CPP-Netlib. 

