```php
<?php
namespace OAuthClient;

class Provider {
    private $scopes = [];

    function __construct(array $config) {
        $this->name = $config['name'];
        $this->clientId = $config['client_id'];
        $this->clientSecret = $config['client_secret'];
        $this->redirectUri = $config['redirect_uri'];
        $this->scopes = $config['scopes'] ?? [];
    }

    public function setScopes(array $scopes): void {
        $this->scopes = $scopes;
    }
}

class OAuthClient {
    private $providers = [];
    private static $instance = null;

    private function __construct() {}

    public static function getInstance(): self {
        if(self::$instance == null) {
            self::$instance = new OAuthClient();
        }
      return self::$instance;
    }

    public function registerProvider(string $name, Provider $provider): void {
        $this->providers[$name] = $provider;
    }

    public function getProvider(string $name): ?Provider {
        if (isset($this->providers[$name])) {
            return $this->providers[$name];
        }
        return null;
    }
}
``` 
This is a simple representation of the OAuthClient library. It uses the Singleton design pattern to ensure only one instance of this class exists in the application. The factory method `registerProvider` allows dynamic registration of providers, and each provider has its own set of scopes. To get an instance of the OAuth client for a specific provider, use the `getProvider` method. 

