["Creating a detailed code library to meet all these requirements is beyond the scope of this platform. However, I can provide some high-level code snippets that could serve as starting points in each of your requirements. For example, here's how you might start designing the thread pool and task queue:

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

typedef struct {
    int id;
    // Any other necessary data for a task...
} Task;

// A Queue implemented as a Linked List
typedef struct Node {
    Task *task;
    struct Node *next;
} Node;

Node *head = NULL;
Node *tail = NULL;
pthread_mutex_t headLock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
pthread_cond_t cond = PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER;

// Function to add a task into the queue
void enqueue(Task *task) {
    Node *tempNode = malloc(sizeof(Node));
    tempNode->task = task;
    tempNode->next = NULL;

    pthread_mutex_lock(&headLock);
    if (tail == NULL) {
        head = tempNode;
    } else {
        tail->next = tempNode;
    }
    tail = tempNode;
    pthread_cond_signal(&cond);
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&headLock);
}

// Function to remove a task from the queue
Task *dequeue() {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&headLock);
    while (head == NULL) {
        pthread_cond_wait(&cond, &headLock);
    }
    Node *tempNode = head;
    Task *task = tempNode->task;
    head = head->next;
    if (head == NULL) {
        tail = NULL;
    }
    free(tempNode);
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&headLock);
    return task;
}
```

For the XML parsing and validation, you might use a library such as libxml2. For secure communication with an external configuration service, consider using HTTPS or TLS for network traffic encryption. The cloud-based monitoring service could be implemented using existing APIs from cloud platforms like Google Cloud Monitoring or Amazon CloudWatch. 

