Here is an example of a function that creates a worker thread pool:
```c
#include <pthread.h>

typedef struct {
    int id; /* Useful debug info */
} thread_args_t;

void* work(void *arg) {
   thread_args_t *args = (thread_args_t*) arg;
   // Perform task here...
   return NULL;
}

// Function to initiate processing of first XML file in queue.
int startProcessing() {
    pthread_t threads[5];  /* 5 is the number of desired workers */
    thread_args_t args[5];

    for (int i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
        args[i].id = i;
        if (pthread_create(&threads[i], NULL, work, &args[i]) != 0) {
            return -1;  /* Failed to create thread */
        }
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
        pthread_join(threads[i], NULL);
    }

    return 0;
}
```
For XML parsing, you can use libxml2 library and the XML C parser. For handling system dependencies, consider wrapping your code's main workflow in a try-catch block to catch any errors or exceptions thrown by the third party service. OAuth 2.0 could be implemented using a library like curl or using the open source project oauth2 library.

