        // Generate structures and populate hash table

        if (!isUniqueRNTI(hashTable, newStructure->rnti)) {
            printf("Duplicate RNTI detected. Logging.\n");

            // Log duplicates
            logError(dbConn); 

            continue;
        }

        // Insert into database
        if (!insertIntoDatabase(dbConn, newStructure)) {
            printf("Failed to insert structure. Aborting.\n");

            rollbackTransaction(dbConn);

            freeMemory(structures, N); 
            closeConnection(dbConn);

            return;
        }
    }

    // Commit transaction
    commitTransaction(dbConn);

    // Clean up and release resources
    freeMemory(structures, N);
    cleanupHashTable(&hashTable); 
    closeConnection(dbConn);
}
```
The actual implementation would require integration with a database library (e.g., libpq for PostgreSQL), the handling of threads and synchronization primitives, logging mechanism and memory management strategies optimized for your system's specific needs. Each part of the function can be developed further depending on how you want to handle it.
