This is a simple controller that accepts POST requests on the `/uploadFile` endpoint, and calls the `AmazonClient` service to upload the received file to Amazon S3 cloud storage. 

The `AmazonClient` service could be as follows:

```java
import com.amazonaws.services.s3.model.PutObjectRequest;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.web.multipart.MultipartFile;

@Service
public class AmazonClient {

    private String BUCKET_NAME = "your-bucket-name";

    @Autowired
    private AmazonS3 s3client;

    public String uploadFile(MultipartFile multipartFile) {
        String fileUrl = "";
        try {
            File file = convertMultiPartToFile(multipartFile);
            String fileName = generateFileName(multipartFile);
            fileUrl = BUCKET_ENDPOINT + "/" + fileName;
            uploadFileTos3bucket(fileName, file);
            file.delete();
        } catch (Exception e) {
           e.printStackTrace();
        }
        return fileUrl;
    }

    private File convertMultiPartToFile(MultipartFile file) throws IOException {
        File convFile = new File(file.getOriginalFilename());
        FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(convFile);
        fos.write(file.getBytes());
        fos.close();
        return convFile;
    }

    private String generateFileName(MultipartFile multiPart) {
        return new Date().getTime() + "-" + multiPart.getOriginalFilename().replace(" ", "_");
    }

    private void uploadFileTos3bucket(String fileName, File file) {
        s3client.putObject(new PutObjectRequest(BUCKET_NAME, fileName, file));
    }
}
```
This is a simplified example and does not include the full complexity of your task. For more complex tasks you might need to consider using frameworks like Spring Cloud for service management, AWS SDK for interacting with cloud services, etc. Also, it's important to handle all potential exceptions in production-grade code and provide comprehensive testing.
']

