['Creating a full library as described in these specifications is beyond the scope of this platform. However, I can provide you an example of a C library that supports AES encryption/decryption with OpenSSL using JSON configuration file for keys and IVs. This code does not cover all your requirements but it's a good starting point:

```c
#include <openssl/aes.h>
#include <jansson.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

typedef struct {
    AES_KEY key;
    unsigned char iv[AES_BLOCK_SIZE];
} CryptoContext;

void init(CryptoContext* ctx, const json_t* json) {
    size_t length = 0;

    // Get key and IV from JSON config.
    const char *key = json_string_value(json_object_get(json, "Key"));
    const char *iv  = json_string_value(json_object_get(json, "IV" ));

    length = strlen(key);
    if (length != AES_BLOCK_SIZE) {
        // Handle error.
    }

    memcpy(ctx->iv, iv, AES_BLOCK_SIZE);
    AES_set_encrypt_key((const unsigned char*) key, length * 8, &ctx->key);
}

void encrypt(CryptoContext* ctx, const unsigned char* in, unsigned char* out) {
    AES_cbc_encrypt(in, out, sizeof(in), &ctx->key, ctx->iv, AES_ENCRYPT);
}

void decrypt(CryptoContext* ctx, const unsigned char* in, unsigned char* out) {
    AES_cbc_encrypt(in, out, sizeof(in), &ctx->key, ctx->iv, AES_DECRYPT);
}
```
This code reads keys and IVs from a JSON configuration file using the Jansson library. It then initializes an encryption context with these values. The `encrypt` and `decrypt` functions use OpenSSL's AES CBC mode to perform encryption and decryption, respectively. Note that this is a basic example and doesn't cover all your requirements but it should serve as a starting point for creating your own library. 

For a more complete solution you need to include additional features such as error handling, logging, command-line interface, thread safety, memory optimization, dynamic resource allocation, anomaly detection system, error correction codes and cryptographically secure IVs generation with optional HSM integration. These would significantly increase the complexity of this code.
